WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.660
India has over 1.4 billion people.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.730
Now imagine removing
almost two-thirds of them!

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.220
Instead of one of the world's
most populated countries,

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.780
India would have just 500 million people.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:11.720
Imagine the difference.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.020
There could be less
pressure on housing, roads,

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.570
public transport and
some natural resources.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.100
Cities might have more space,

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.240
and infrastructure could
face different demands.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.550
But there's another side.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.040
India would also have a
much smaller workforce,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:27.220
fewer consumers and potentially
a very different economy.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.590
A smaller population doesn't
automatically mean a richer country.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.210
Would you prefer a less crowded
India with 500 million people,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.310
or today's India with over a billion?

